{
  "$schema": "https://turbo.build/schema.json",
  "extends": ["//"],
  // WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. Two `apps/server` unit tests are censuses of files OUTSIDE this package,
  // and turbo hashed neither — so each could be served a cached green after its subject changed.
  // This is the same defect `deploy/airgap/turbo.json` and `tools/helm-verify/turbo.json` document,
  // found by sweeping every package rather than by fixing the one that was reported.
  //
  //   - `src/governance/scan-db.test.ts` — "EXPECTED_TRIVY_DB_SCHEMA_VERSION matches
  //     tools/trivy/pin.env byte-for-byte". A PIN-DRIFT GATE whose whole point is that the constant
  //     in this package and the pinned scanner agree; bumping `TRIVY_DB_SCHEMA_VERSION` in
  //     `tools/trivy/pin.env` alone changed no file turbo hashed for `@scp/server`. This is
  //     structurally identical to the measured `@scp/plugin-managed-scan` defect, where an
  //     all-zeros `ARG TRIVY_IMAGE=` digest went `>>> FULL TURBO`, 5/5 cached, green.
  //   - `src/openapi/build-document.test.ts` — reads the COMMITTED `tools/openapi/openapi.v1.json`
  //     precisely so a route that stopped being registered fails here rather than only in an E2E
  //     job. The emitted contract is regenerated by `pnpm gen`, which is a different task in a
  //     different package: nothing about that regeneration invalidates this package's `test` hash.
  //
  // `$TURBO_DEFAULT$` MUST STAY FIRST. Declaring `inputs` REPLACES the default package-scoped set;
  // omitting it would leave this package's own `src/**` unhashed, which trades a narrow staleness
  // for a total one.
  //
  // Keep this list in step with the tests. If a census here grows a new out-of-package subject, its
  // path belongs here, or that census passes on a cached green exactly once and then stays wrong.
  "tasks": {
    "test": {
      "dependsOn": ["build"],
      "inputs": [
        "$TURBO_DEFAULT$",
        "$TURBO_ROOT$/tools/trivy/pin.env",
        "$TURBO_ROOT$/tools/openapi/openapi.v1.json"
      ]
    }
  }
}
